---
/**
 * The transparency section almost no competitor has. The example numbers are
 * clearly labeled as an illustration — they are not a quote or a real deal.
 */
---

<div class="grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <div class="reveal">
    <span class="eyebrow">No black box</span>
    <h2 id="math-heading" style="font-size: var(--text-h2)">How we calculate your offer</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
      Most cash buyers keep their math secret. We don't. Every offer we make comes from the same
      simple formula — and we'll walk you through your numbers on the phone:
    </p>
    <p class="card mt-5 !bg-brand-950 text-center font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">
      Your offer = what the fixed-up house will sell for<br />
      − repair costs − our costs &amp; margin
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-slate-700">
      <li class="flex gap-2.5">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-bold text-brand-600">✓</span>
        <span><strong>The fixed-up value</strong> (the "after-repair value") comes from real sales of similar homes near yours — not a guess.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-2.5">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-bold text-brand-600">✓</span>
        <span><strong>Repair costs</strong> are what we'll actually spend. We've renovated houses all over Columbus — see our <a href="/before-after/" class="font-semibold text-brand-700 underline">before &amp; after projects</a>.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-2.5">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-bold text-brand-600">✓</span>
        <span><strong>Our costs &amp; margin</strong> cover buying, holding, and reselling the house, plus a fair profit for the risk we take. That margin is how we stay in business without charging you anything.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card card-lift reveal !p-7" style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
    <p class="text-sm font-bold tracking-widest text-clay-600 uppercase">Example only — not a quote</p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Every house is different. Here's the shape of the math:</p>
    <dl class="mt-5 space-y-3.5 text-base">
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-4 border-b border-slate-100 pb-3">
        <dt class="text-slate-700">House value after repairs</dt>
        <dd class="font-bold text-slate-900">$220,000</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-4 border-b border-slate-100 pb-3">
        <dt class="text-slate-700">− Repairs (roof, kitchen, paint…)</dt>
        <dd class="font-bold text-slate-900">$40,000</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-4 border-b border-slate-100 pb-3">
        <dt class="text-slate-700">− Our costs &amp; margin</dt>
        <dd class="font-bold text-slate-900">$40,000</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-4 rounded-xl bg-brand-50 px-4 py-3">
        <dt class="font-bold text-brand-900">Your cash offer</dt>
        <dd class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-brand-900">$140,000</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      And from that number, <strong>nothing is subtracted</strong> — no 6% commission, no closing
      costs, no repair credits. If a higher price on the open market makes more sense for you,
      we'll say so. Some people should list with an agent. We'd rather tell you the truth than buy
      your house.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
